    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2024387161760371033",
      "url": "https://x.com/iSabongera/status/2024387161760371033",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/iSabongera/status/2024387161760371033",
      "text": "VP SARA DUTERTE’S ACHIEVEMENTS AS VICE PRESIDENT \n\nA growing narrative pushed by kakampinks, NPA fronts, enablers, and Marcos apologists claims that Sara Duterte has accomplished nothing as Vice President. This claim is false.\n\nDespite repeated budget cuts and sustained harassment against OVP personnel, the Office of the Vice President of the Philippines has continued to implement and expand programs launched since 2022. \n\nThese programs directly address transportation, livelihood, education, health, disaster relief, and food security—delivering measurable results nationwide.\n\nBelow is a clear breakdown of key programs and outcomes as of July 2025:\n\nMag Negosyo Ta ’Day\n\nLivelihood Assistance\n • 30 groups assisted\n • 1,416 individuals assisted\n • Total beneficiaries: 1,446\n\nValue for Money\n • Average grant per group: ₱150,000\n • Average grant per individual: ₱15,000\n • Total program cost: ₱36,434,000*\n\nMedical and Burial Assistance (Individuals Assisted)\n\nMedical\n • 2022: 15,417\n • 2023: 95,756\n • 2024: 154,406\n • Total: 265,579\n\nBurial\n • 2022: 4,998\n • 2023: 24,368\n • 2024: 32,891\n • Total: 62,257\n\nValue for Money\n • Total individuals assisted: 327,836\n • Average assistance per individual: ₱6,128\n • Total program cost: ₱2,032,957,000*\n\nPagbaBAGo: A Million Learners and Trees Campaign\n\nSchool Bags Distributed\n • 2022: 3,820\n • 2023: 156,495\n • 2024: 227,958\n • 2025: 15,547\n • Total: 403,820\n\nTrees Planted\n • 2023: 451,104\n • 2024: 182,982\n • 2025: 308,338\n • Total: 942,424\n\nValue for Money\n • Total program cost: ₱141,244,000\n • Average cost per learner: ₱349.77\n\nLibreng Sakay Program\n\nPassengers Served\n • 2022: 238,743\n • 2023: 638,625\n • 2024: 1,025,275\n\nValue for Money\n • Average cost per passenger: ₱14.33\n • Total program cost: ₱34,627,000*\n\nRIICE (Relief for Indigents and Individuals in Crisis and Emergencies)\n\nFamilies Served\n • 2022: 694\n • 2023: 11,240\n • 2024: 144,808\n • 2025: 40,479\n • Total: 197,221\n\nKalusugan Food Truck\n\nFirst Responders Served\n • 2023: 3,311\n • 2024: 2,055\n • 2025: 1,230\n • Total: 6,596\n\nSo, those who are saying that VP Sara has done nothing as Vice President is either uninformed or simply dumb.\n\n-Tio Moreno\nhttps://t.co/dj07phiPjd",
